{"kind":"artifact","text":"Implementation of request 2a9f7da5 at cmd/gs@1843fd90bee09c37619df1996d7078635683f82a on branch request/invalid-advertisement-fail-closed, recut onto current main 4fc94b0f. Fulfils my promise e636faa5. Companion to the internal/app artifact 29ae11fb, which carries the typed read this consumes.\n\nWHAT CHANGED. resolveServerURL previously did `advertised, published := workspace.ResidentURL(); if !published { return \"\", nil }`, and an empty server URL means fold locally. It now reads the tri-state: NoAdvertisement returns the local fold exactly as before, AdvertisementPublished validates and uses the address exactly as before, and AdvertisementUnusable returns an error naming which failure it was and offering --server - to act locally on purpose.\n\nREFUSAL HAPPENS BEFORE KEY CUSTODY, which was the condition that mattered most. Refusing after loading a signing key, or after appending, is not refusing. resolveServerURL already ran before the key load in all six write commands; that was true but unenforced, so it is now pinned by TestAnUntrustworthyAdvertisementRefusesBeforeAnyKeyIsRead. That test fails if a key read is moved ahead of resolution — I verified it by doing exactly that and watching all nine of its subtests fail with \"the advertisement was resolved after the key was read\".\n\nCOVERAGE OF ALL ELEVEN SERVER-AWARE COMMANDS. TestEveryServerAwareCommandRefusesAnUntrustworthyAdvertisement runs each of the six writes (state, review, merge, ratify, supersede, batch) and five reads (status, work, artifacts, inspect, reviews) three times with identical arguments: with a foreign-genesis record advertised at a live counting listener, the same plus --server -, and with the record deleted. Every command refuses in the first case with the resolver's own words, dials the listener zero times, and for the six writes leaves head and depth unchanged. Every command gets past in the other two.\n\nTHE TEN CLASSES, EACH PINNED TO ITS OWN GUARD. Nine untrustworthy classes — unreadable, oversized, not a record, truncated, empty address, missing genesis, foreign genesis, malformed address, non-loopback address — plus absence, which must still act locally and is held by TestNoAdvertisementActsLocally. --server - is held by TestServerDashForcesTheLocalFold. A well-formed advertisement at a dead address is held by TestAnAdvertisedAddressThatRefusesTheDialAppendsNothing, which asserts the refusal says nothing landed.\n\nWHY EACH TEST ASSERTS ITS OWN GUARD'S REASON STRING, which is the part I would most like a reviewer to check. I removed the resolver's AdvertisementUnusable branch — the actual fix — and five of the nine classes STILL produced an error, because ValidateURL caught the fallthrough with different words. A suite asserting only \"the command refused\" would have passed with the fix deleted. So each class asserts the substring only its own guard produces. I confirmed this by removing that branch and watching all eleven command subtests fail; and separately removed the 8 KiB bound, the empty-address check and the genesis comparison one at a time, each failing only its own class. I ran those four mutations myself rather than reporting the implementing agent's account of them.\n\nTHE UNREADABLE CLASS CANNOT SILENTLY PASS. It chmods the record to 0000, which does not stop a caller that bypasses file permissions; under such a caller the subtest would pass while never reaching the branch it claims to pin. It now reads the file back and skips loudly if it can. I proved the guard fires by making the record readable and watching the class SKIP with a named reason rather than pass.\n\nGATES at this exact head: gofmt clean; go build ./... and go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... over the whole module with zero failures; ./internal/docset green at -count=1.\n\nLayer 7. The CLI contract changes: an untrustworthy advertisement is a refusal rather than a silent local fold. Documented in the same head under the docs artifact. Absent-advertisement and explicit --server behaviour, including the - sentinel, are unchanged.\n\nONE HONEST LIMIT. The dead-address refusal is fail-closed because submitRequest has no local-fallback path, which predates this change. I did not add a mutation for \"the local fallback was reintroduced\", because that is removal of an absence rather than of a guard, and I would rather say so than imply coverage I did not build.","body":{"commit":"1843fd90bee09c37619df1996d7078635683f82a","path":"cmd/gs"}}